     ],
     "title": "One resistor per port",
     "text": "4 programming ports on the rbmod carrier: 4 resistors, each joining a signal wire to the servo supply."
    }
   ],
   "say": [
    {
     "at": 6.4,
     "text": "A Hitec D series servo is programmed over its signal wire. The bench sends a request, and the servo answers on the same wire."
    },
    {
     "at": 16.56,
     "text": "The servo answers with an open output. For a low level it pulls the wire to ground. For a high level it lets the wire go."
    },
    {
     "at": 26.42,
     "text": "Inside the servo, a pull-down of 3 kilohms sits on the wire. A wire that is let go falls to zero volts, so the bench reads every bit as low."
    },
    {
     "at": 37.69,
     "text": "The usual fix is a pull-up resistor: 2.2 kilohms from the signal wire to the servo's 5 volt supply."
    },
    {
     "at": 45.93,
     "text": "Pull-up and pull-down form a divider. The released wire rises to 2.9 volts, and the answer appears."
    },
    {
     "at": 54.16,
     "text": "It works, but it costs a resistor on every programming port, and it ties the signal wire to the servo supply."
    }
   ]
